The vulnerability:
- `vcardstructured_new_from_string` in vcardstructured.c
- For each `;` in the input, it does `st->field[st->num_fields++] = field;`
- `field[]` array has `VCARD_MAX_STRUCTURED_FIELDS = 20` slots (indices 0-19)
- The first field is added at index 0 (num_fields becomes 1)
- Each `;` adds another field, incrementing num_fields
- After 20 `;` characters, num_fields would be 21, and `st->field[20]` would be an out-of-bounds write (index 20 is out of bounds for a 20-element array)

Wait, let me re-read the code carefully:

```c
vcardstructuredtype *vcardstructured_new_from_string(const char *str)
{
    struct vcardstructuredtype_impl *st = vcardstructured_alloc();
    if (!st) {
        return st;
    }
    vcardstructured_ref(st);

    vcardstrarray *field = vcardstrarray_new(2);
    st->field[st->num_fields++] = field;   // first field at index 0, num_fields=1

    do {
        char *dequoted_str = vcardvalue_strdup_and_dequote_text(&str, ",;");

        if (*str == ',' || field->num_elements || strlen(dequoted_str)) {
            vcardstrarray_append(field, dequoted_str);
        }
        icalmemory_free_buffer(dequoted_str);

        if (*str == ';') {
            /* end of field */
            field = vcardstrarray_new(2);
            st->field[st->num_fields++] = field;   // each ';' adds a field
        }

    } while (*str++ != '\0');

    return st;
}
```

So:
- Initial: field at index 0, num_fields = 1
- 1st ';': field at index 1, num_fields = 2
- ...
- 19th ';': field at index 19, num_fields = 20 (this is the last valid index)
- 20th ';': field at index 20, num_fields = 21 → OUT OF BOUNDS WRITE

So I need 20 semicolons in the JSCOMPS parameter value to trigger the OOB write at index 20.

Actually wait, the crash is "Heap-buffer-overflow WRITE 8". Writing a pointer (8 bytes on 64-bit). So writing `st->field[20]` which is past the end of the array.

The struct:
```c
struct vcardstructuredtype_impl {
    unsigned refcount;
    size_t num_fields;
    vcardstrarray *field[VCARD_MAX_STRUCTURED_FIELDS];  // 20 elements
};
```

So `field[20]` writes past the end of the struct allocation. That's the heap-buffer-overflow WRITE 8.

